From 11403089e90f2358702fc6bc0f6218d39a209e79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Newton <rrnewton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 08:21:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Stage crates.io publish-readiness: bump 0.0.0->0.2.0 + add
 descriptions

Refreshed onto current main (post PR #1196 hermit-cli 0.2.0 + third-party-
backends feature gate + reverie->reverie-core rename on the reverie side).

- Bump every workspace crate version 0.0.0 -> 0.2.0 (package versions and
  internal path-dep requirements); hermit-cli already 0.2.0 via #1196, only its
  internal dep reqs bumped here.
- Add crates.io 'description' to the 11 publishable crates that lacked one.

Deliberately NOT included: the reverie git->version->registry dep rewrite. On
main those deps are already dual {version, git, rev}; the real-publish rewrite
(strip git+rev, point at published reverie-core via a package alias) is an
owner step documented in crates-squat-staging/REAL-PUBLISH-ORDER.md, because it
cannot dry-run clean until reverie is on a registry.

Validation (cargo 1.97.1, dry-run --no-verify): hermit leaves
test-allocator/hermit-resources/digest/edit-distance package clean (digest name
collides with RustCrypto -> rename); reverie-dependent crates gate solely on
'no matching package named reverie-syscalls found' (reverie not yet published).
This is a staging validation vehicle, not for direct merge.
